/* CHORD VOLLEYS: when two scoring arrivals land on the SAME whole beat, the second one rings harmony instead of the
   same note twice. Two module scalars are the whole state machine — the beat the last scoring arrival landed on and
   how many have landed on it — read on the heard timeline (voiceQ/bowNote's correction) so what the tracker calls
   "the same beat" is the beat the player HEARD. The chord itself is one triggerAttackRelease on `pad`, at the same
   beatSnap the kill note took, from the ACTIVE theme's own CHORD_TRIAD: no new voice, no new node, no scheduling,
   no rnd() draw, and nothing here is ever read by score, streak, grading or ghostRec.
   THE CLANK-MUTE DOES NOT REACH HERE (SPEC §3, v1.1 amendment): the mute's blast radius is the LEAD KILL-NOTE and
   nothing else, ever. A volley earned during a mute still rings its dyad/triad on `pad` — the muted kill's own lead
   note staying silent IS the cost, and silencing the harmony too would charge one clank twice. */
